---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Why Choose Portland Sheep?" description="Why Portland sheep are well suited to smallholders, conservation grazing, showing, meat and wool production.">
  <div class="bg-sage-800 text-white py-20 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-sage-300 text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">About</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl mb-6">Why Choose Portland Sheep?</h1>
      <p class="text-cream-200 text-xl max-w-2xl">A historic, versatile breed with character, excellent wool and a natural place on today's smallholding.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <nav class="flex gap-4 mb-12 border-b border-cream-200 pb-4 overflow-x-auto">
      {[['Overview', '/about/'], ['Why Portlands?', '/about/why-portland-sheep/'], ['History', '/about/history/'], ['Wool', '/about/wool/'], ['For the Table', '/about/for-the-table/']].map(([label, href]) => (
        <a href={href} class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-500 hover:text-sage-700 pb-4 -mb-4 border-b-2 border-transparent hover:border-sage-500 transition-colors whitespace-nowrap px-1">{label}</a>
      ))}
    </nav>

    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:text-sage-800">
      <p>Portland sheep are a breed steeped in history and remain a popular choice for smallholders. Their manageable size, hardy nature and distinctive appearance make them rewarding sheep for both new and experienced keepers.</p>

      <h2>A useful and adaptable breed</h2>
      <p>Portlands can breed outside the conventional autumn season, a valuable characteristic that has been passed to other Dorset breeds. Their modest size and ability to make use of lower-quality grazing allow them to fit well into small farms and conservation-grazing projects. They still need attentive year-round husbandry, suitable forage and normal preventative health care.</p>

      <h2>Wool, meat and showing</h2>
      <p>The soft, creamy fleece is sought after by hand-spinners and other fibre craftspeople. Slowly grown Portland hogget and mutton is known for fine texture and a distinctive depth of flavour. In the show ring, Portlands are generally calm, manageable and full of character, making them suitable for novice and young handlers as well as experienced exhibitors.</p>

      <h2>Full of character</h2>
      <p>Above all, Portlands are striking and personable sheep. Their tan faces, red-coated newborn lambs and elegant horns give the breed its unmistakable appearance. With appropriate handling—and often the encouragement of a feed bucket—they can become friendly and engaging members of a flock.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
